// The played bed -- the mix the owner actually plants, 2026-09-09.
//
// Every headless figure in the lab's reports before this was taken on the
// harness default: eight herb founders of one species, and (until `ants_at`)
// a colony dropped on seedlings at frame 0. The owner does not play that
// box. They grow a mixed bed first and then add ants, and the difference is
// not cosmetic -- same binary, same seed, a colony founded at frame 0 holds
// 4-13 animals at 30,000 frames where one founded at 6,000 holds 31.
//
// **The mix is the owner's own, given 2026-09-09: grass, herb and shrub.**
// Each does a different job, which is the whole reason a mix is not just a
// denser lawn:
//
//   grass  -- the fast ground staple. No separate leaves, matures in 10, and
//             it keeps the bench lit: measured over 120,000 frames a grass
//             bed holds 0.562 of lamp light at the soil where herb falls to
//             0.240 and shrub to 0.110.
//   herb   -- the only shipped plant that sets fruit, matures in 60.
//   shrub  -- slow woody clumps, matures in 250. These are what make the bed
//             patchy rather than uniform, so distance to food is a real
//             quantity in it.
//
// **No tree, and that was measured rather than assumed.** A tree was in the
// first reading of the owner's answer, so it was rendered before anything
// was run on it: one tree founder becomes 79 plants and shades the bench to
// **0.008** of lamp light by frame 30,000 -- thirty times darker than the
// herb bed, with the low plants that actually feed a colony shaded out. A
// long run on a bed with a tree in it measures the canopy closing, not
// whatever else it was pointed at. Review card
// `20260909T232116894Z-2b3661` puts the choice to the owner; if the answer
// is "tree anyway", it is one more `Plant` line here and every figure taken
// on this file has to be retaken.
//
// **Thirteen plants, and a bare band in the middle, both measured rather
// than chosen.** A grown bed physically refuses a colony: `found_colony_of`
// needs bare footing, and by frame 6,000 the vegetation and its seed litter
// have taken the surface. Measured at frame 6,000, founders seated out of
// the 52 asked for:
//
//   bare bed, no plants at all                     52
//   22 plants spread evenly across the bed          8
//   13 plants spread evenly across the bed         23
//   13 plants with none in the nest band 210..310  33
//
// So the band is not decoration. A colony dropped on a full bed is a colony
// of eight, and a run of it reads as a breeding rule that does not fire --
// `CLAUDE.md`'s "a scene that contradicts the code will look like a bug in
// the code", and the founder count is the only line in the output that says
// so. A player does this by eye anyway: you place a nest on bare ground.
//
// A `Clear` sweeping the band immediately before founding was tried and is
// NOT here: it bought 3 more founders (36 against 33) and cost three grown
// plants, so it is a worse bed for a rounding error.
//
// Seating still varies a lot with the seed -- 33, 13 and 18 on seeds 1, 2
// and 3 -- because where the seed litter falls is where the nest cannot go.
// That spread is a real property of the played bed and belongs in any
// figure taken on it.
//
// **The colony arrives at frame 6,000, on the timeline.** That is the whole
// point of the file -- `Colony` in `timeline` rather than `placements` is
// what makes this the played bed instead of the harness one, and it is why
// `ants_at=` is ignored in scenario mode: the timeline decides.
(
    name: "played_bed",
    title: "THE PLAYED BED",
    question: "The mix the owner plants -- grass, herb and shrub grown for 6,000 frames, then a colony lands on it.",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 25),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 50),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 75),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 105),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 130),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 155),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 180),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 330),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 355),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 380),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 410),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 435),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 465),
    ],
    timeline: [
        // **Clear the nest site one frame before the colony lands.**
        //
        // Without this the scenario asks for 52 founders and `found_colony_of`
        // seats **8**: by frame 6,000 a grown grass bed has laid ~750
        // ungerminated seeds across the surface, every one of them an
        // occupied cell, and a colony needs bare footing. The run then reads
        // as a colony that will not breed, which looks exactly like a broken
        // breeding rule and is nothing of the kind -- `CLAUDE.md`'s "a scene
        // that contradicts the code will look like a bug in the code",
        // caught by the founder count and by nothing else in the output.
        //
        // A player does this by eye: you click bare ground. The band is 112
        // columns of the bed's middle, cleared to 8 rows above the soil,
        // which is where the seed litter sits.
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
    ],
    horizon: 120000,
)
